 "assign": {
  "about": "Which species a surveyed tree is drawn as (v2/data/scene/tree_species.py; in order: register, osm, named, type, water, street, wood, park). register: the tree of the city's register nearest to the surveyed tree, within register_m of it (the register's point is the trunk, the survey's the crown's top); such a tree also takes its type (conifer, red-leaved, green) from its species. A mix given as a list takes the species' register shares as weights; one given with numbers takes those. named: streets and squares whose trees are known (the city's register, by place, 24 Nov 2026). wood: the wooded valley slopes are mixed broadleaves, mostly sycamore and ash, with oak and some beech (the city's forest service points in the centre; the reading of their codes is ours). water: by judgment (the register lists 92 weeping willows in the city, among them those of the Pétrusse and the Alzette).",
